#: includes/class-abilities.php:180
msgid "List content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:181
msgid "Search and paginate posts in a REST-enabled post type, most recently modified first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:188
msgid "Only this status. Default: every status except trash."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:193
msgid "Sort field. Default modified."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:198
msgid "Sort direction. Default desc (asc for title)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:214
msgid "Read content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:215
msgid "Read a post by ID, URL or slug: raw Gutenberg markup, terms, featured image, SEO meta, the builder that stores its layout, your autosave if any, and the content hash needed for updates. Pass autosave_content to read the text of your staged autosave."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:220
msgid "Permalink of the post, as an alternative to post_id."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:221
msgid "Post slug, as an alternative to post_id. Combine with post_type for pages or custom types."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:223
msgid "Also return the title, content and excerpt of your autosave. Edits to live posts are staged there, so read it back after such a save."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:230
msgid "Save content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:231
msgid "Create a draft or update a post through WordPress. Updates need the current content hash from get-content. Edits to a published, private or scheduled post are saved as your autosave for review unless you pass status (for example publish) to change the live post. Publishing or scheduling always requires status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:235
msgid "Post to update. Omit to create a post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:236
msgid "Post type for a new post. Default post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:237
msgid "Plain-text title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:238
msgid "Complete post content, usually serialized Gutenberg block markup. Replaces the existing content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:239
msgid "Manual excerpt."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:242
msgid "New status. Omit to keep drafts as drafts and stage edits to live posts. future needs a future date_gmt."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:245
msgid "URL slug. WordPress makes it unique."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:246
msgid "Publish date in UTC, ISO 8601, for example 2026-10-05T09:00:00Z. A future date with status publish or future schedules the post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:249
msgid "Replace terms per taxonomy, for example {\"category\": [3], \"post_tag\": [\"seo\", 12]}. Integers are term IDs; strings are names, created when missing. Use list-terms to find IDs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:259
msgid "Image attachment ID for the featured image, or 0 to remove it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:262
msgid "Post meta to set, for example SEO title and description fields. Only keys listed in get-content meta support are accepted; an empty string deletes the value."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:268
msgid "content_sha256 from get-content. Required for updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:275
msgid "List terms"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:276
msgid "Find categories, tags or other taxonomy terms and their IDs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:280
msgid "REST-enabled taxonomy such as category or post_tag. Default category."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:293
msgid "List media"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:294
msgid "Find existing media library items with their URLs, alt text and dimensions. Prefer existing media over new uploads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:298
msgid "Filter by MIME type or family, for example image or image/png."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:311
msgid "List skills"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:312
msgid "List the bundled page builder skills (Gutenberg, GenerateBlocks, Elementor, Bricks, Divi) and skills that active plugins add, such as store or invoicing workflows, with whether each applies here and its files. Read the matching skill before creating or editing builder layouts or before running a plugin's workflow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:338
msgid "Read skill"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:339
msgid "Read a skill from list-skills: a bundled page builder skill or one an active plugin adds. Start with its SKILL.md, which explains the workflow and which reference files to read next."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:343
msgid "Skill name from list-skills."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:344
msgid "File within the skill, for example references/elements.md. Default SKILL.md."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:359
msgid "List Bricks abilities"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:360
msgid "List Bricks Builder's own abilities on this site: name, label, one-line summary, readonly and destructive hints, and the tool name of those also served directly (bricks-*). Pass ability_name for the full description and the input and output schemas. Use this where Bricks guidance names mcp-adapter-discover-abilities or mcp-adapter-get-ability-info."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:364
msgid "A Bricks ability, for example bricks/get-page-elements, to return in full with its schemas."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:365
msgid "Only list abilities whose name, label or description contains this text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:392
msgid "Run Bricks ability"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:393
msgid "Run one of Bricks Builder's own abilities with its parameters. Use this where Bricks guidance names mcp-adapter-execute-ability; ability_name and parameters work the same way. Bricks checks its own permissions and validates the parameters against the ability's input schema. Abilities that are not readonly change the site: follow Bricks' readback and revision guidance."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:397
msgid "Bricks ability name from bricks-abilities, for example bricks/get-page-elements."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:398
msgid "The ability's input, matching its input schema. Omit for abilities that take no input."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:411
msgid "Upload media"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:412
msgid "Import a file into the media library from a public URL or base64 data, with alt text. WordPress checks the file type. Use the returned ID as featured_media or the URL in content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:416
msgid "Public http(s) URL to import. Private and loopback addresses are refused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:417
msgid "File contents as base64, up to 10 MiB. Requires filename."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:418
msgid "File name with extension, for example hero.png. Required with data_base64."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:419
msgid "Optional post to attach the media to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:427
msgid "Update media"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:428
msgid "Set the title, alt text, caption or description of an existing media item."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:438
msgid "List source files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:439
msgid "Browse plugin, theme and must-use plugin directories. Hidden files, credential files and symlinks are hidden."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:443
msgid "Directory relative to wp-content, for example plugins or themes/my-theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:444
msgid "Entries to skip. Default 0."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:447
msgid "Entries to return, 1 to 200. Default 100."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:465
msgid "Read source file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:466
msgid "Read a UTF-8 plugin or theme source file up to 256 KiB and obtain the SHA-256 hash needed to change it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:483
msgid "Write source file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:484
msgid "Create or replace a plugin or theme source file. Supply its current hash, or new for a new file. PHP is syntax- and compile-checked first; after saving, the site is loaded and a change that causes a fatal error is reverted. This changes executable code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:489
msgid "Complete new file contents."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:490
msgid "sha256 from read-file, or new to create a file that must not exist yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:505
msgid "Create directory"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:506
msgid "Create a directory, and any missing parents, inside plugins/, themes/ or mu-plugins/."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:509
msgid "Directory relative to wp-content, for example plugins/my-plugin/includes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:523
msgid "Delete source file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:524
msgid "Delete a plugin or theme file whose hash still matches, or an empty directory. Deleting PHP that breaks the site is undone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:529
msgid "sha256 from read-file, or directory to delete an empty directory."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:543
msgid "Move source file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:544
msgid "Rename or move a plugin or theme file whose hash still matches. The destination must not exist. A PHP move that breaks the site is undone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:548
msgid "Current path relative to wp-content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:549
msgid "New path relative to wp-content. Its directory must exist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:564
msgid "Execute PHP"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:565
msgid "Run PHP statements in the loaded WordPress request with full server privileges; not sandboxed. No PHP tags and no exit or die. Echo output and a JSON-serializable return value are captured; errors include their message and line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:568
msgid "PHP statements without <?php, for example: return get_option( \"blogname\" );"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:580
msgid "Run WP-CLI"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: time limit in seconds.
#: includes/class-abilities.php:582
#, php-format
msgid "Run WP-CLI on this installation as the authenticated user, with arguments as an array and no shell. Full developer access; foreground commands have a %d-second limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:588
msgid "Command words and flags without the leading wp, for example [\"plugin\", \"list\", \"--format=json\"]. --path, --url, --user, --ssh, --http, --require, --exec, --allow-root and @aliases are set by Site Agent."
msgstr ""

