#: includes/class-admin.php:111
msgid "Enable Site Agent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:111
msgid "Allow authenticated administrators to connect and use the tools selected below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:112
msgid "URL authentication"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:112
msgid "Not recommended. Allow Base64-encoded username and Application Password credentials in the MCP endpoint auth query parameter. The password is only encoded, and URLs can be recorded in client history, chats and server logs. Use OAuth connections instead whenever the client supports them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:113
msgid "OAuth connections (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:113
msgid "On by default. Let MCP clients that support OAuth, such as Claude and ChatGPT connectors, connect by signing in here. An administrator approves each client on a consent screen and picks its tool groups. Clients get one-hour access tokens and refresh tokens that end after 30 days without use. No password is shared with the client."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:114
msgid "Content writes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:114
msgid "Create drafts, edit posts or pages, set terms, featured images and SEO fields, and import media. Edits to live posts are staged as autosaves unless a status is passed explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:115
msgid "Source inspection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:115
msgid "Read plugin, theme and must-use plugin source files. Source files can contain sensitive data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:116
msgid "Source editing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:116
msgid "Create, overwrite, move or delete plugin and theme files, including PHP. PHP changes that cause a fatal error are reverted when the site can be checked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:117
msgid "PHP execution"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:117
msgid "Run PHP inside WordPress with the server process privileges. This is not a sandbox and can modify files, the database, and Site Agent itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:118
msgid "WP-CLI execution"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:119
msgid "Bricks tools"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:119
msgid "Serve Bricks Builder's own abilities (Bricks 2.4 or later, with AI/MCP enabled in Bricks > Settings > AI): its fast-path tools directly and the rest through one dispatcher. They can change pages, templates, global classes, variables, theme styles and Bricks settings. Bricks' own switches and permission checks still apply, and its PHP ability also needs PHP execution."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:120
msgid "Audit history"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:120
msgid "Keep the last 100 tool calls: time, user ID, tool, target (post ID, file path or WP-CLI command name), Application Password name, result and duration. Content, code, other arguments, outputs, IP addresses and credential secrets are not logged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:121
msgid "Delete data on uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:121
msgid "Remove Site Agent settings, password limits, audit history and the update license when deleting the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:127
msgid "Site Agent requires site administration rights, or super administrator rights on multisite."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:143
msgid "Connect your AI client directly to this WordPress installation. Site Agent has no hosted proxy and makes no telemetry requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:145
msgid "SITE_AGENT_DISABLED is active. All Site Agent access is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:148
msgid "WordPress file modification or editing is disabled. Source inspection, source editing, PHP, and WP-CLI tools are blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:151
msgid "SITE_AGENT_ALLOW_EXECUTION is false in wp-config.php. Source editing, PHP, and WP-CLI tools are blocked on this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:162
msgid "Unavailable: Bricks abilities are not active. They need the Bricks theme 2.4 or later with AI/MCP enabled in Bricks > Settings > AI."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:164
msgid "Blocked by a wp-config.php constant on this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:175
msgid "Connect a client"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:177
msgid "Enable Site Agent and the tools you need, and keep OAuth connections on. Save."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:178
msgid "Add the endpoint below to your MCP client, such as a Claude or ChatGPT connector, Claude Code or Cursor, with no credentials."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:179
msgid "The client opens a WordPress sign-in and consent page. Check the client name, choose the tool groups it may use, and allow it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:181
#: includes/class-admin.php:263
#: includes/class-diagnostics.php:32
msgid "Endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:182
msgid "Application Passwords (not recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:183
msgid "Use an Application Password only for a client that cannot sign in with OAuth. It acts as your account until you revoke it, every client configuration that holds it can leak it, and a password in a URL can also end up in history, chats and server logs. OAuth tokens expire, can be limited per client, and never reveal a password."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:185
msgid "Create a dedicated WordPress Application Password in your profile, one per client."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:186
msgid "Use the endpoint above in a client that supports Streamable HTTP and a custom Authorization header. The header uses HTTP Basic authentication with your username and Application Password. Keep the client configuration private, and limit the password's tools above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:188
msgid "Remote connections require HTTPS. Plain HTTP is accepted only when WordPress identifies the installation as local. Clients that require OAuth can connect with the endpoint alone once OAuth connections are on: they find the sign-in page through the endpoint's OAuth metadata."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:190
msgid "Connect with an authenticated URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:191
msgid "If your MCP client cannot send a custom Authorization header, include your credentials in the endpoint URL instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:193
msgid "Enable Site Agent and URL authentication above, select the tools you need, then save your settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:194
msgid "Create a dedicated Application Password in your administrator profile."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:195
msgid "Enter your WordPress username and that Application Password in the converter below. Click Generate token, then Copy authenticated endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:196
msgid "Paste the copied URL into your client as a Streamable HTTP MCP endpoint. The client must retain the auth query parameter on every request; a separate Authorization header is not required."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:198
msgid "Example format only: BASE64_TOKEN is a placeholder for the encoded username:application-password value. The copy button generates and URL-encodes it for you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:200
msgid "Keep the complete URL private."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:200
msgid "Base64 is reversible. This URL contains credentials and may appear in browser history, client configuration or server logs. Site Agent removes it from the request before other plugins run their late logging, but earlier server logs can still record it. Use a dedicated Application Password and clear the converter after copying."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:201
msgid "To stop URL-based connections, turn off URL authentication and save. To revoke this credential everywhere, revoke its Application Password in your profile; existing MCP sessions cannot bypass revocation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:202
msgid "A compatible Streamable HTTP MCP client is required. Prefer OAuth connections for clients that support them: no credential appears in a URL. ChatGPT web compatibility with credential-bearing URLs has not been verified."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:206
msgid "Each tool switch controls that entry point. PHP execution, executable source editing, and WP-CLI can change other settings or files, so these switches are not isolation boundaries. Use a backed-up development or staging site for developer tools."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:207
msgid "To revoke remote access, disable Site Agent or revoke its Application Password in your profile. For an emergency stop, set SITE_AGENT_DISABLED to true in wp-config.php; set SITE_AGENT_ALLOW_EXECUTION to false to block only source editing, PHP and WP-CLI. Deactivation also disables access until you enable it again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:225
msgid "OAuth connections are off, so clients can only connect with an Application Password. Turn OAuth connections on below; it is the recommended way to connect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:228
msgid "URL authentication is on. A password in a URL is only encoded and can be recorded in client history, chats and server logs. Reconnect those clients with OAuth, then turn URL authentication off and revoke their Application Passwords."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: Application Password names.
#: includes/class-admin.php:241
#, php-format
msgid "Tool calls in the last 30 days used Application Passwords (%s). Reconnect those clients with OAuth if they support it, then revoke the passwords in your profile."
msgstr ""

